      "message": "This changes the behaviour. In a previous patchset, the code wouldn\u0027t return but go ahead and renew the cert with the existing key, known to be good to sign.\n\nYou return 0 now, which makes it retry \"signer, ok :\u003d tlscert.PrivateKey.(crypto.Signer)\" again and again, until \"next\" is \u003c\u003d dr.m.renewBefore()+renewJitter at which point it\u0027ll branch out to renewing the cert with the original key anyway.\n\nSo, maybe it\u0027s better to fallback to the original behaviour: return next, nil to use existing cert?",
